## Deep Research Lineage Complete — glm-devin

**Lineage:** `glm-devin` (executor: cli-devin / glm-5-2)
**Spec folder:** `specs/cli-external-orchestration/045-cli-pi-bridge-cursor-devin/001-research-bridge-possibilities`
**Write surface:** `research/lineages/glm-devin/`
**Iterations:** 5 of 5 (stop policy: max-iterations)
**Questions answered:** 5/5
**Key findings:** 27
**Ruled-out directions:** 6
**Verdict:** **not-feasible-now**

### Summary

No path to natively expose Cursor and Devin subscription-backed models in Pi's `/model` picker is both technically clean and account-safe as of August 2026:

| Path | Verdict | Evidence |
|------|---------|----------|
| P1 Built-in Pi Cursor/Devin provider | Ruled out (iter 1) | No built-in provider in `providers.md` or live `auth.json` |
| P2 Cursor token-reuse HTTP | Ruled out (iter 2) | Cursor staff ruling + ToS §1.5; account ban risk; `api2.cursor.sh` is private Connect-RPC |
| P3 Devin token-reuse HTTP | Ruled out (iter 3) | Cognition ToS §2.3 analog; `credentials.toml` is full account credential; `api.devin.ai` v3 is session REST |
| P4 Reverse-engineered proxy | Ruled out (iter 4) | ToS §1.5(i); exemplar `Cursor-To-OpenAI` uses reverse-engineered protobuf |
| P5 CLI-spawn gateway | Not recommended (iter 4-5) | Technically feasible but ToS-ambiguous; nested-harness breaks Pi tool loop; duplicates existing `cli-cursor`/`cli-devin` executor |

**Recommendation:** Do not build a native Pi Cursor/Devin bridge now. Keep the existing `cli-cursor`/`cli-devin` executor dispatch as the supported surface. Track two vendor feature requests: (1) Cursor public OpenAI-compatible `/v1/chat/completions`, (2) Devin raw-completions surface. Re-evaluate when either ships.

